ore: `msg = \"This is an example exception\"` / `raise RuntimeError(msg)`\n- After: `msg_0 = \"This is an example exception\"` / `raise RuntimeError(msg_0)`\n\nThe `defaults.snap` also added a new EM101 diagnostic block for the regression test (at `EM.py:118:28`), showing the fix produces `msg_0 = \"!\"` and `raise RuntimeError(msg_0)`, preserving the existing `msg = \".\"` binding.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe PR's goal, per its title, is to \"Avoid shadowing existing `msg` in fix for `EM101`\". The refactor relocated the `fresh_binding_name` helper into shared `edits.rs` so both the `flake8-errmsg` and `ruff` rules can reuse it, ensuring generated variable names don't collide with existing scope bindings.", "durationMs": 13224, "url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/24363/files"}

